WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.744
Every animal has a covering
on the outside of its body.

2
00:00:07.964 --> 00:00:13.722
Fur, feathers, scales or skin.
Different animals have different ones.

3
00:00:14.222 --> 00:00:17.984
A cat has fur. Soft hair
all over, to keep it warm.

4
00:00:18.204 --> 00:00:22.105
A bird has feathers. They are
light and warm, and help it fly.

5
00:00:22.325 --> 00:00:26.179
A fish has scales. Small
hard plates that overlap.

6
00:00:26.399 --> 00:00:31.276
A frog has smooth, wet skin.
No fur, no feathers, no scales.

7
00:00:31.496 --> 00:00:35.396
You have skin, with hair on your
head. You are an animal too.

8
00:00:35.896 --> 00:00:40.540
Sorting by covering puts animals with
the same kind of outside together.

9
00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:45.172
A dog has fur. A duck has
feathers. A crocodile has scales.

10
00:00:45.392 --> 00:00:50.826
A penguin swims, but it is not a
fish. It is a bird, with feathers.

11
00:00:51.046 --> 00:00:54.111
Look at the outside of the
animal, not where it lives.

12
00:00:54.611 --> 00:00:58.512
A cat and a dog both have
four legs, two ears and fur.

13
00:00:58.732 --> 00:01:02.400
But a cat has claws it can
pull in. A dog does not.

14
00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:05.964
Animals are alike in some
ways and different in others.

15
00:01:06.464 --> 00:01:10.690
A hen starts as an egg. The egg
hatches, and a chick comes out.

16
00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:15.601
The chick grows bigger and grows
feathers. Now it is a young hen.

17
00:01:15.821 --> 00:01:20.232
The young hen grows into a grown
hen. She lays eggs of her own.

18
00:01:20.452 --> 00:01:24.725
A baby cannot walk or talk. A
child can. A grown-up is taller.

19
00:01:24.945 --> 00:01:28.521
People change as they grow,
just like other animals.

20
00:01:29.021 --> 00:01:33.758
Puppies look like their parents. A
spotty mother, and a brown father.

21
00:01:33.978 --> 00:01:37.786
The puppies: one spotty, one
brown, one brown with spots.

22
00:01:38.006 --> 00:01:41.721
Not exactly like the mother,
and not exactly like the father.

23
00:01:41.941 --> 00:01:45.145
Each puppy gets its own
mix from both parents.

24
00:01:45.645 --> 00:01:48.246
A picture shows what an animal looks like.

25
00:01:48.466 --> 00:01:52.135
A diagram is a drawing with
labels that name the parts.

26
00:01:52.355 --> 00:01:55.002
This one names the wing,
the beak and the legs.

27
00:01:55.222 --> 00:01:58.890
It leaves out colours on
purpose, so the parts stand out.

28
00:01:59.110 --> 00:02:02.501
Scientists draw diagrams
to show what matters.

29
00:02:03.001 --> 00:02:07.134
Every animal has a covering:
fur, feathers, scales or skin.

30
00:02:07.354 --> 00:02:12.183
Sort them by covering. They are alike
in some ways, and different in others.

31
00:02:12.403 --> 00:02:16.629
Young animals change as they grow,
and get a mix from both parents.

32
00:02:16.849 --> 00:02:20.518
A diagram names the parts.
A picture shows the look.
